{"id": "33dfb626-8045-4f60-98c8-3fa8a3240992", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T18:11:05.364979", "source": "user", "parent_id": "5e2c755f-5e87-4e8c-81d4-92f997dd487f", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Hi, before we go anywhere near the actual design, I want a grounded look at what we're working with. Please do the following and nothing more:\\n\\n1) Inspection: check /workspace for anything relevant to this study — any PDF model code/implementation (the \\\"period\\\" mechanism, e.g. patch/period length hyperparameters), an ETTm1 dataset or dataloader, existing configs, and any prior experiment scripts or results. Report what exists and what is absent. If the repo is empty (which the project notes hint at), say so plainly.\\n\\n2) Proposed approach: sketch how you would structure a design-only experiment answering \\\"how do different period settings affect PDF model performance on ETTm1\\\". At minimum outline: the factor (period setting and candidate values), what \\\"period\\\" means in this model (patch length? seasonal period? both?), baselines/controls, dataset split convention for ETTm1 (standard 12-month train / 2-month val / test split), forecast horizons to evaluate (e.g. 96/192/336/720), metrics (MSE/MAE), seeds/repeats, and feasibility notes given no GPU and no installed dependencies.\\n\\n3) Assumptions & uncertainties: list every consequential assumption explicitly — e.g. which PDF variant/architecture we assume, whether we fix other hyperparameters or co-tune them, lookback window choice, and anything else you can't confirm from the source material. I'm skeptical by default, so don't paper over gaps: unknown means unknown, write it down.\\n\\nDo NOT produce the full final design yet. I want the inspection report, the skeleton approach, and the assumption list first, then we'll review and green-light the main work.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How do different period settings affect the performance of the PDF model on the ETTm1 dataset?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
