offsets.\n- Horizons 96/192/336/720 with seq_len 96 (standard) or 336 (PatchTST uses 336 for long-term).\n- Metrics: MSE and MAE (mean over channels, samples, horizons; also per-horizon reporting), normalization: instance norm (RevIN) or dataset-standard scalers fit on train.\n- Seeds: 3 seeds (e.g., 0,1,2) or 5; report mean±std; note literature convention of 1 seed and the risk.\n- Selection: model selection on val MSE with fixed patience/early stopping, and decide whether period tuning happens on val (that's the honest way to answer \"effect on performance\") — separate \"fixed-hyperparameter effect\" vs \"best-period selection\".\n- Feasibility: no torch, no numpy, no network, no GPU → cannot run; design-only. Estimate compute: ETTm1 69,680×7, seq 96→720, PatchTST-like model ~ few M params; a single run ~ minutes-to-an-hours on 1 GPU / tens of minutes CPU. Total runs: #periods(~10) × horizons(4) × seeds(3) = 120 runs → note that this is feasible on a single GPU overnight-ish, and reduce options (share a model across horizons per PatchTST practice? no — one model per horizon).\n\nAlso the answer must include: what we'd need to obtain (PDF code, ETTm1 CSV, dependency install) — currently blocked by no network; so design must include a provisioned environment step.\n\nAlso note the possibility of a cheap CPU-only proxy check: implement a numpy-free pure-Python FFT/ACF to estimate dominant periodicities of ETTm1 to justify candidate period values — but no numpy; pure Python DFT on a 1440-sample downsample is doable. But we don't have the dataset. So that's a \"when data available\" check.\n\nOne more feasibility note: the workspace is a tmpfs (1TB, RAM-backed) — artifacts should be persisted elsewhere or exported; and files there are ephemeral. Also 224 CPUs available which helps CPU-only training with small models.\n\nNow write the plan handoff. It must include: inspection report, skeleton approach, assumptions & uncertainties. Keep organized but thorough.\n\nLet me also double check there's no hidden dir or git repo.\n\nAlready: find /workspace -maxdepth 3 showed only task.json. Good.\n\nLet me now compose. Also include a list of clarification questions (budget 6) — I'll ask the key ones, though researcher_topics is empty; I can still pose questions in the handoff.\n\nI'll structure the end_researcher_turn answer with sections. Evidence will contain raw observations.\n\nNote: I should be careful about asserting the ETTm1 split numbers; present as \"commonly used convention to be pinned from source\" with uncertainty.\n\nAlso state metrics convention: scaled (standardized by train mean/std) MSE/MAE — standard in the TFT/PatchTST protocol; the Informer/Autoformer repos report MSE/MAE on standardized data (scalers fit on train). PatchTST/RevIN reports on normalized. Flag it.\n\nCompute the number of runs. Grid: periods 10 × horizons 4 × seeds 3 = 120, plus controls ~ 4 conditions × 4 horizons × 3 seeds = 48. Plus co-tune patch_len grid if 2-factor: 10 periods × 3 patch lens × 1 horizon(720?) × 2 seeds = 60. Total ≈ 230 runs. Note reduction strategies.\n\nWrite it out.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "## 1) INSPECTION REPORT — the repo is empty. Plainly.\n\nWhat exists in /workspace: exactly one file, `task.json` (389 bytes), containing the question, a context string, and a note `\"track.md\": \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"`\n\nWhat is ABSENT (all verified, not assumed):\n- **PDF model code / paper / PDF-related PDFs: none.** No `.py`, no `.ipynb`, no `exp_main.py`, no `models/`, no `configs/`, no docs. Therefore I cannot read the \"period\" mechanism, cannot see its hyperparameter name (`period`? `patch_len`? `period_len`? `num_periods`?), its default value, or whether it interacts with patching/stride/padding.\n- **ETTm1 dataset / dataloader: none.** No `ETT-small/`, no `ETTm1.csv`, no `data_provider/`, no `.csv` anywhere. Whole