lue both logged. Secondary (small) 2-factor sweep: period \\u00d7 patch_len {8, 12, 16} at horizon 720 only, to show whether period effects are confounded with tokenization. Also pre-declare that hyperparameter selection uses the **val** split only, and report both (i) the effect curve at fixed shared settings and (ii) the best-on-val period per horizon, since these answer slightly different questions.\\n\\n**2h. Feasibility (stated, not glossed).** As delivered here, **nothing can be executed**: no torch/numpy, no dataset, no network to fetch either, no GPU. The design is therefore explicitly *design-only*, plus a provisioning preflight (obtain PDF source + ETTm1 CSV + deps offline; verify file row count and channel order; record exact split constants from the dataloader). Sizing: ~9 period levels \\u00d7 4 horizons \\u00d7 3 seeds \\u2248 108 runs + ~50 control/2-factor runs. On a single modern GPU a small patch-based forecaster on ETTm1 is minutes per run \\u2192 overnight-ish; CPU-only is plausible for this model size given 224 cores but is a separate risk. Trim path if needed: 2 seeds and horizons {96, 720} first.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3) QUESTIONS I NEED ANSWERED (6-question budget; these are blocking)\\n1. Which PDF is this (paper title/venue/repo), and can you supply the source or the model file? Nothing is in /workspace.\\n2. What does `period` mean in that code \\u2014 mechanism A, B or C above \\u2014 and is it in raw timesteps or patch units?\\n3. What are PDF's published/default ETTm1 settings (seq_len, patch_len, stride, d_model, e_layers, dropout, lr, epochs/patience, normalization: RevIN vs train-standardization)?\\n4. Does the code *auto-derive* period (FFT/ACF) so a manual override even exists? If not, the factor isn't directly manipulable and we need a code-patch, which changes the design.\\n5. Multivariate (all 7 channels) or univariate HUFL only, and is the reported metric the standard 4-horizon average or per-horizon?\\n6. Where should artifacts/results be written, given `/` is tmpfs?\", \"evidence\": \"DIRECT OBSERVATIONS (all commands run in this session):\\n\\n1. `ls -la /workspace` \\u2192 only `task.json` (389 bytes, owner 154547). `find /workspace -maxdepth 3` \\u2192 `/workspace` and `/workspace/task.json` only. No subdirectories, no hidden files, no `.git`.\\n2. `cat /workspace/task.json` \\u2192 {\\\"question\\\":\\\"How do different period settings affect the performance of the PDF model on the ETTm1 dataset?\\\",\\\"context\\\":\\\"Design an experiment... Do not claim that an experiment was run.\\\",\\\"documents\\\":{\\\"track.md\\\":\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"}}. Note: `documents.track.md` is a string in JSON, not a file on disk (no track.md exists in /workspace).\\n3. `find / -xdev \\\\( -iname \\\"*ETT-small*\\\" -o -iname \\\"*ETTm1*\\\" -o -iname \\\"*PatchTST*\\\" -o -iname \\\"*time-series-library*\\\" \\\\)` \\u2192 no output (empty). No ETT data or reference forecaster repos anywhere on the filesystem.\\n4. `python3 -c \\\"import numpy, pandas, torch\\\"` \\u2192 ModuleNotFoundError. Individually confirmed: `No module named 'numpy'`, `No module named 'torch'`. `ls /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages | grep -Ei \\\"numpy|pandas|torch|scipy\\\"` \\u2192 empty. `pip list` = Debian system packages (ansible 13.1.0, Jinja2, cryptography, ...); no scientific/ML stack, no gluonts/transformers/scikit-learn/scipy.\\n5. Python version: 3.14.4 (GCC 15.2.0).\\n6. GPU: `ls /dev | grep -i nvidia` \\u2192 no match; `which nvidia-smi` \\u2192 command not found. No CUDA devices.\\n7. Network: `urllib.request.urlopen('https://pypi.org')` \\u2192 `URLError: <urlopen error [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution`. Cannot pip-install or download ETTm1.\\n8. Compute/storage: `nproc` \\u2192 224. `df -h /` \\u2192 `tmpfs 1006G 0 1006G 0% /` (RAM-backed; artifact persistence risk).\\n9. No GPU and no deps \\u21d2 no experiment can be executed here; consistent with the task.json note that \\\"repositories and compute are not required\\\".\\n\\nINFERENCE FLAGGED AS INFERENCE: the ETTm1 10-minute sampling \\u21d2 144 steps/day, 1008 steps/week, and the 12-month/2-month/remainder split convention come from my prior knowledge of the Informer/Autoformer/PatchTST ETTm1 protocol, NOT from anything in this repo, which contains no dataloader and no CSV. Row count ~69,680 and the exact split constants must be re-derived from the actual file/loader when obtained.\", \"assumptions\": [\"PDF = a deep long-horizon forecaster with an explicit, manually settable 'period' hyperparameter. UNVERIFIED \\u2014 no PDF source exists in /workspace.\", \"'period' is expressed in raw timesteps (not patch units) and is independent-ish of patch_len. UNVERIFIED; if mechanism A (patch-position embedding) holds, period and patch_len/stride are entangled and the grid must be re-expressed in patch units.\", \"Mechanism ambiguity A/B/C is unresolved and is treated as an open question, not as an assumption already settled.\", \"ETTm1 = the standard 7-channel 10-minute file with the 12-month train / 2-month val / remaining test convention, borders shifted by seq_len, targets standardized with train-fit scaler. Convention asserted from prior literature, not from repo code.\", \"Multivariate forecasting over all 7 channels with MSE/MAE averaged across channels; 4 horizons 96/192/336/720, one model trained per horizon; primary seq_len 96 (secondary 336).\", \"All non-period hyperparameters are fixed at one declared configuration for the main sweep; a small period \\u00d7 patch_len sweep handles the confound separately. If the researcher prefers per-cell co-tuning, the design must be restructured (and the answer becomes 'best-achievable vs period', not 'effect of period').\", \"\\u22653 seeds per cell with a pre-registered significance rule; published single-seed ETT tables are not treated as a reliable effect-size reference.\", \"A code patch may be required if PDF auto-derives period from data and exposes no override. In that case the 'period' factor becomes an intervention on the estimator, not a config knob.\", \"No experiment is run or claimed in this deliverable; feasibility numbers are planning estimates only.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Identity of 'PDF' and its architecture \\u2014 completely unknown from the provided material; the whole design hinges on it.\", \"Exact semantics of 'period' (patch-position period vs. seasonal/decomposition cycle vs. patch length itself) and its units; also whether it must divide the lookback, be a multiple of stride, or be capped by seq_len.\", \"Whether period can be disabled at all (needed for the `none` control) or whether the control must be implemented as a code ablation.\", \"Whether seq_len=96 (standard) is even valid for periods \\u2265144 \\u2014 with a lookback shorter than one daily cycle, high period levels may be no-ops, which could produce a spurious 'no effect' result.\", \"Exact ETTm1 file length, channel order, missing-value handling (the published ETT files contain NaNs) and the split constants used by the PDF authors; normalization choice (RevIN vs train standardization) changes reported MSE by more than some plausible period effects.\", \"Whether published PDF results on ETTm1 exist and under which protocol \\u2014 needed to know whether our absolute numbers should be comparable to a table or only internally comparable across period levels.\", \"Unknown target metric direction of interest: best average over horizons vs best at long horizons (period effects are commonly horizon-dependent).\", \"Compute budget and wall-clock allowance for the real run are unspecified; my 108+ run sizing may exceed what the researcher can spend, and the trim path (2 seeds, horizons {96,720}) would weaken the seed-level variance estimate.\", \"Storage: / is tmpfs, so run artifacts may vanish unless an export location is designated.\", \"Dependency availability offline: even with 224 CPUs, no torch/numpy means nothing runs today; provisioning is a hard prerequisite, not a footnote.\"], \"summary\": \"Inspect empty workspace, propose period-experiment skeleton and assumptions\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-a5f86a89-80e8-9af2-aa8f-8f153f6e0fa9", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Inspect empty workspace, propose period-experiment skeleton and assumptions", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
